	(text "MCU MODULE: OSPTEK ESP32-P4C5 Core (ESP32-P4 rev v3.x + ESP32-C5HF4, 16 MB flash, 32 MB PSRAM).\nInside the module: SDIO on P4 GPIO14-19, C5 CHIP_PU = P4 GPIO54 (pad 82), C5 GPIO2 = P4 GPIO6 (pad 21, NC here)\n- the same wiring as the Waveshare reference board. Pins: bsp/include/bsp/board_pins.h.\n3.3 V supply (3V3_MCU, shunt RS404 / PM2 CH2). RTC_VBAT from VBACKUP (always on): P4 RTC keeps time when off.\nCHIP_PU has no RC inside the module: R607/C607 here. C5 reset from the Dev port via R606 onto the GPIO54 net.\nWi-Fi: module IPEX -> U.FL-U.FL jumper -> J601 -> J602 RP-SMA on the RF edge (50R). LAN_OUT pad unused.\nHand solder: 1.0 mm stamp holes; no exposed copper/untented vias under the module.\nGPIO35 = BOOT strap + RMII TXD1 (4.7k pull-up, PHY must not pull it low at reset).\nSW603 SLEEP/WAKE -> GPIO12 (LP GPIO): press = expander rails off + P4 deep sleep; press again = wake (ext1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 233.68 0)
		(effects
